> I've got a package "A" that has a runtime dependency to a configuration f=
ile. This configuration file is image specific. For each image I've got a s=
pecific configuration package "config-image-X" that installs this needed co=
nfiguration file and I build multiple image in the same build directory.
> How can I enforce that each image containing package "A" also installs an=
 image specific configuration package?

If the "config" package is image-specific, you could just invert the=20
dependency. Make the config package RDEPEND on "A". Images that install the=
=20
config (which they have to do anyway according to your description) will th=
en=20
automatically install "A" which at least accomplishes that you don't need t=
o=20
specify both.

I've been in the same position, and it just isn't possible to do what you w=
ant.




